{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Var.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.toPoly?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">Cutsat</span>.<span class=\"name\">toPoly?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.GoalM\">GoalM</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Linear.html#Int.Internal.Linear.Poly\">Poly</a>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the polynomial `p` of `e` if `e` is in the normal form produced by the `grind` preprocessor,\nand `none` otherwise. The normal form is a left-nested sum of monomials `k * a` (`k ∉ {0, 1}`) or\n`a`, followed by an optional nonzero numeral, where no atom `a` is decomposed by `toLinearExpr`.\nFor terms in this form, `p.denote'` is definitionally equal to `e` by unfolding.\n\nTerms in dependent positions may not be in normal form because the preprocessor cannot rewrite\nthem. The caller must normalize them using `toLinearExpr` and `Int.Internal.Linear.Expr.norm`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Var.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.toPoly?","kind":"def","line":167,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.toPoly?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Var.lean#L167-L196"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arit